{
  "_comment": [
    "Test data for an MCP instance's seed vault. Rows are inserted in the order",
    "of TABLES in the app's schema.ts (parents before children); within a table",
    "they go in file order, except tasks, which are inserted twice so a subtask",
    "can point at a parent that comes later.",
    "",
    "Columns are filtered against PRAGMA table_info, so a column the app drops",
    "later is ignored rather than failing the build. Anything the app defaults",
    "sensibly is left out on purpose - this file should read as data, not as a",
    "restatement of the schema.",
    "",
    "@@chip(id,entryType,label)@@ in a content string expands to a real internal",
    "link chip via the app's own internalLinkChipHtml(), so the markup cannot",
    "drift from the editor extension.",
    "",
    "Ids are written readable (seed-wiki-sigil) and become stable UUIDs at build",
    "time, everywhere they occur: the app only follows links to UUIDs. Write a",
    "new row's id as seed-<something> and reference it by that name.",
    "",
    "Entries of every module, tags, categories and tasks carry one deleted row each so the trash is",
    "testable without having to delete something first. Their deleted_at is moved",
    "to about a day before the build, so the trash retention does not purge them."
  ],

